// The SOLUTION ROOT. It lists the projects; it checks nothing itself.
//
// `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` therefore checks ZERO FILES and exits 0 —
// measured, and it cannot be made to refuse: `files: []` and `include: []` both
// exit 0 with no output (bug-root-tsconfig-passes-vacuously). So the fix is to
// make the command that DOES work complete, and to keep it complete:
//
//     npm run typecheck        →  tsc --build tsconfig.json, every project below
//
// A project missing from `references` is invisible to that command, which is
// how `tsconfig.mcp.json` and `tsconfig.tests.json` went unchecked by it.
// `tests/unit/tsconfigReferences.test.ts` fails if a tsconfig.*.json in this
// repo is not listed here.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.web.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.mcp.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.tests.json" }
  ]
}
